      "Use a short readiness script to print the working directory, runtime version and entry file during early exercises. Remove it when no longer useful, but keep the habit of proving context before diagnosing an import or file-not-found error.",
      "Pause at the line before the incorrect value appears, then move forward one operation at a time. Inspect values and types without editing them in the console first; changing paused state can be useful, but it also changes the experiment you are observing.",
      "Name tests after the observable rule, such as `rejects an empty title`, rather than the function name alone. When a failure occurs, the test report then explains which promise to the caller was broken.",
      "Before committing, run the public scripts from a fresh terminal and read the entire diff. This catches accidental generated files, debug statements and secrets while the change is still local and easy to correct."
